rotein content is bucketed into our  amino oncology bucket with over 140  targets for human and mouse  and a neuroscience bucket with over 75  targets  for our human i o content we are about  to release three new panels you'll see  them at the  on the bottom left in the i o space  those are the map case signaling panel  the pi 3k akt signaling panel  and the cell death panel our content is  designed in a core and module format and  you'll see this illustrated on the right  you have to choose a core module with  about 20 plex  with additional controls and that can be  a human i o core  a mouse io core or a human neural core  you then have the choice to add up to  six different ten plex  modules onto that core lastly if you'd  like  you can add an additional 10 custom  antibodies  bringing you to 96 plex for your  experiment  now i'd like to look in a little more  detail at the i o content  for our human immuno oncology portfolio  again we have that core  it's here in the green table and the  core is  one of our broad broad panels it'll  allow  it includes key immuno oncology targets  and markers of immune cells  including t cells b cells and  macrophages  on the right hand side of the slide  you'll see four of our seven total  modules we'll go through the next three  in a moment of these four  modules again they're all approximately  10 plex  the cell typing module is the most broad  the cell typing module can allow you to  profile a range of specialized cell  types including macrophages  and regulatory t cells  next the immune activation status module  can help you more deeply profile immune  exhaustion  the io drug target module includes  additional checkpoint and immune  modulatory targets that are currently  under development for io therapies  some of those targets such as pdl-1 are  in the core but this module includes  additional targets that might be of  interest to you  and lastly on this slide our pan tumor  module can allow you to more deeply  profile the tumor  here on the right hand side you'll see  our three new human io modules that'll  be released shortly they're going  through our validation process now which  i'll talk about short in a moment  the map case signaling module and the  pi3k akt  signaling module will both be of  interest to those who are studying  targeted therapies against  one of these pathways and they both  include phosphorylated protein products  that  measure pathway activation  lastly our cell death module will allow  you to profile the tumor  um and and mediators of immunogenic and  programmed cell death  for our mouse models out there our mouse  immuno oncology portfolio includes the  core  and four total modules  those are the immune cell typing module  the immune activation status  io drug target and pan tumor later this  year we'll also be expanding this  content  to match what uh the human io content  that we've just gone over to include  those two new signaling  pathway panels and the cell death panel  as i mentioned earlier all of the  antibodies that we offer commercially  go through a thorough validation process  i'd like to show you some data from that  now  our validation process is broken down  into five steps shown here  on the left you see the first step which  is an ordering screen here we  validate our off-the-shelf antibodies in  control tissue  next they go through a post conjugation  screen to test the specificity of the  conjugated antibody  the third step we go through a  sensitivity and specificity screen  then an interaction screen to make sure  all the antibodies will work  in combination with one another and  finally we go through  a tma screen to make sure to  ensure that the antibodies perform as  we'd expect in real tissue  now looking at each of these steps with  some data from antibodies from our three  new  human i o panels here we show the pre  and post conjugation screen  on the top row of all of these um ihc  images  you'll see our unconjugated antibodies  